%T A341473 736343647428517997,22960108096994524441028
%N A341473 The number of antitransitive relations on n labeled nodes.
%C A341473 A relation is antitransitive if xRy and yRz implies "not xRz". As such, antitransitive relations are always irreflexive.
%C A341473 Let G be the simple support graph of an antitransitive relation. Every edge of G that belongs to a triangle is singly oriented, every triangle is cyclically oriented, while an edge belonging to no triangle may be oriented in either direction or in both directions. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 02 2026
%H A341473 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intransitivity#Antitransitivity">Intransitivity</a>.
%F A341473 Let G range over the unlabeled simple graphs on n vertices. Let q(G) be the number of edges of G contained in no triangle, and let t(G)=|E(G)|-q(G). For each triangle-edge {i,j}, i<j, introduce x_ij in GF(2), with x_ij=1 denoting i->j. For every triangle i<j<k impose x_ij=x_jk and x_ik=1-x_ij. If this affine system is consistent of rank r(G), then G contributes (n!/|Aut(G)|)*3^q(G)*2^(t(G)-r(G)); otherwise 0. Hence a(n) is the sum of these contributions over G. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 02 2026
%Y A341473 Number of relations on labeled nodes: A000110 (equivalence), A002416 (unrestricted), A006125 (symmetric), A006905 (transitive), A047656 (reflexive and antisymmetric), A083667 (antisymmetric), A341471 (antisymmetric and antitransitive).
